#: templates/index.html:147
msgid "The Problem"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:148
msgid "The Numbers We Don't See"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:149
msgid ""
"The waste crisis in Mexico is present every day. Here are some data "
"points about the problem we face:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:155 templates/index.html:173 templates/index.html:186
#: templates/index.html:199
msgid "day"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:157
msgid "of waste collected per day in Mexico during 2022"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:158
msgid "National average · 32 states · Collected waste only"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:161
msgid ""
"Equivalent to <strong>862 grams per person per day</strong>. Half of all "
"waste collected in the country comes from just 6 states: Mexico City, "
"State of Mexico, Jalisco, Veracruz, Nuevo León and Guanajuato. "
"Additionally, <strong>150 municipalities had no collection "
"service</strong> — in those places, burning garbage was the most common "
"practice."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:165 templates/index.html:178
msgid "Source:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:165
msgid "INEGI — Cuentame, Environment (2022)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:174
msgid "generated daily by the state of Michoacán"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:175
msgid ""
"Of the total generated in the state, <strong>less than 2&#37; is effectively "
"recycled</strong>. The rest is deposited, burned or abandoned without "
"treatment."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:178
msgid "Michoacán Ministry of Environment"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:187
msgid "in Pátzcuaro, only 64 reach the landfill"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:188
msgid ""
"<strong>36 daily tons</strong> don't reach any treatment system: they end"
" up in clandestine dumps, water bodies or streets. Pátzcuaro was the site"
" of our 2024 pilot test."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:191 templates/index.html:204
msgid ""
"Official communication, Ecology Department, Municipality of Pátzcuaro "
"(2024)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:200
msgid "generated on average by each resident of Pátzcuaro"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:201
msgid ""
"Less than a kilogram. A bag, a bottle, a package. But multiplied by every"
" person, every day, it is the accumulation you experience in your "
"surroundings."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:211
msgid "The five oceanic plastic islands"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:213
msgid "km² of combined surface area"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:217
msgid "Mexico"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:224
msgid "Plastic Islands"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:233
msgid ""
"The problem is not a single plastic \"island\" floating in the ocean, but"
" five large accumulation zones where millions of plastic fragments "
"concentrate due to ocean currents. Together, <strong>they cover an area "
"equivalent to more than eight times Mexico, making cleanup extremely "
"difficult and putting entire ecosystems at risk</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:239
msgid ""
"The data describes what <span class=\"bridge-muted\">gets "
"collected</span>. What <strong>NuestroEntorno</strong> maps is what "
"<strong>nobody went to look for</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:240
msgid ""
"Waste that never reached the garbage truck. Trash dumped in an empty lot,"
" a ravine or a riverbank. Accumulations in places where municipal "
"services never arrive and that, therefore, don't appear in any official "
"statistics. Those are the points we document, and they are not harmless. "
"They are active hotspots of damage to the people and surroundings of "
"those who live nearby."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:245
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:246
msgid "What illegal dumps generate"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:251
msgid "Infection Hotspots"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:252
msgid ""
"The accumulation of organic waste attracts rats, mosquitoes and flies "
"that spread diseases directly in the spaces where we live."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:257
msgid "Fire Hazard"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:258
msgid ""
"Dry waste and gas accumulation create conditions for spontaneous or "
"deliberate fires that are difficult to control."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:263
msgid "Toxic Gases"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:264
msgid ""
"Decomposition releases methane, CO₂ and toxic compounds (greenhouse "
"gases) that degrade air quality in nearby areas."
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:269
msgid "Aquifer Contamination"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:270
msgid ""
"Leachates (toxic liquids from waste) seep into the soil and reach "
"underground aquifers. <strong>Much of the water we consume daily comes "
"from there.</strong>"
msgstr ""

#: templates/index.html:278
msgid ""
"Every report in <strong>NuestroEntorno</strong> turns the invisible into "
"data. One report at a time."
msgstr ""

